  (text "Limb: 4 low-side channels. Muscle wire k runs from the +10 V hole to hole Wk. W1/W2 and W3/W4 are the antagonist pairs." (at 20 30 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid efc58ab9-9dc0-4ba2-b41b-c6707b3d8bf7))
  (text "Flyback diodes may be fitted DNP if the wire leads are short. Gate pull-downs keep every MOSFET off when the 74HC595 outputs are disabled." (at 20 34 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 680b5e07-6cd7-4563-9bad-8f6f7906e3f6))
  (text "AO3400A pins: 1 G, 2 S, 3 D (SOT-23)." (at 20 38 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid e384a0bd-1423-4ccd-a5fb-1d384e972538))
  (text "Gate guard (hardware, no software involved): CAC AC-couples the drive, RPD bleeds it, the BAT54 clamp restores the low level each cycle." (at 20 42 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid e386ca8e-0c69-435b-92a1-a03c84012fd1))
  (text "Normal pulses (up to ~250 us) pass with a few percent droop; a gate stuck high decays below threshold in ~3 ms (22 nF x 100 k). Use 100 nF with IRLZ34N." (at 20 46 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 9007fd73-c15a-4b2e-b778-b74cec2dce7b))
)
